doc/ - LaTeX report
===================

An IEEE-conference write-up of the *logical* design: PE datapath, mesh, control
FSM, dataflow mappings and a wire-level cost model - diagrams, no code dumps.

Layout
------
    main.tex        document root: title, abstract, \input of each section
    config/         modular preamble (packages, colours, tikz, macros, hyperref)
    src/            one .tex per section (see src/README)
    figures/        standalone TikZ pictures (see figures/README)
    IEEEtran.cls    vendored, so it builds without a full TeX Live

Build (make -f doc.mk)
----------------------
    make -f doc.mk          latexmk -> build/main.pdf
    make -f doc.mk clean

The PDF ships a hyperlinked outline: it opens with the bookmark pane (the side
"table of contents") visible, one entry per section/subsection, plus PDF
metadata. That is configured in config/hyperref.tex.

nix: `nix develop` provides texliveSmall; the report uses only widely available
packages (hyperref, bookmark, tikz, booktabs, microtype).
